# Skin LAB Editorial — Brand System (machine-readable spec)

> Visual + verbal system for **Skin LAB Editorial**, a European/Americas skincare-intelligence
> account on Instagram & TikTok. Outputs feel like a **scientific journal crossed with a European
> editorial magazine**. Not a beauty blog. Not a pharmacy. A publication.
> Identity in one line: **the intelligence of a lab, the eye of a magazine.** One word: **discernment.**
> Subtitle / tagline (confirmed): **“Ingredients, decoded.”**
>
> The full visual reference is **`Skin LAB Brandbook.html`** (open it to see every rule applied).
> When generating any post, slide, carousel, or video, obey the rules below.

## Positioning & pillars
- **Essence:** Discernment — to see clearly despite the noise.
- **Persona:** a Parisian dermatologist who reads *The Gentlewoman* and has a studio in the Marais. Informed, refined, never clinical, never cute.
- **Audience:** educated, skeptical readers who have outgrown the noise (they know niacinamide from panthenol).
- **Goal:** attract → inform → retain → convert credibility into PR partnerships. No paid reviews; gifting never compromises the copy.
- **Three pillars:** (1) **Earned clarity** — make complexity legible without making it simple; start from evidence. (2) **Editorial conviction** — have a point of view and defend it; opinion is not bias. (3) **Quiet luxury of knowledge** — intelligence is the only status signal; restraint is the luxury marker.
- **Manifesto (north star):** “Most skincare content is made to sell you something. We are not selling anything… We tell you exactly what we found — not what a brand paid us to say, not what an algorithm rewarded. What the evidence says. We exist for the moment after the confusion.”

## Logo & identity
- **Primary wordmark:** “Skin Lab” in **Fraunces** Regular (tracking −20, leading 1.4, 137pt) above “EDITORIAL” in **Proxima Nova** Regular, all caps (tracking +442, leading 1.4, 46.4pt — ~0.34× the name). Three colourways: Ink on Bone (default), Frost on Sage, Sage on Bone. Asset files in `assets/logo-wordmark-*.png`.
- **Seal / secondary mark:** circular molecular stamp reading “SKIN LAB EDITORIAL” (top arc) + “INGREDIENTS, DECODED” (bottom arc) around a 4-node molecule. Two colourways: Ink on Bone, Frost on Sage (`assets/logo-stamp-*.png`). Use as the IG/TikTok **avatar**, TikTok end card, stickers, and any context too small for the full lockup.
- **Isotype:** the 4-node molecule alone, hand-inked/textured (`assets/logo-isotype.png`). The most reduced mark — app icon, favicon, embossing, single-colour stamp. Ink on light, or knocked out in Bone/Frost on Ink or Sage.
- **Clear space:** cap-height of “S” on all sides. **Minimum width** for full lockup ~120px; below that use the seal or the name alone.
- Never re-set the wordmark in another face, stretch/outline/shadow it, or use pure-white / pure-black versions.
- Web rendering: Fraunces loads live; **DM Sans substitutes for Proxima Nova** in the tracked caps (identical at this tracking).

## Molecular pattern
- A tone-on-tone background texture derived from the seal's 4-node molecule. Tiles in `assets/pattern-molecule-*.png` — two colourways (**sage**, **bone/cloud**) × two densities (scattered, dense).
- **Backgrounds only.** Story panels, cover fills, the TikTok end card, packaging tissue. Keep it *barely there* — it must never compete with type or photography, and live text never sits on the dense version. Web utility: `.bg-molecule` (or set the tile as a `background-image`, `background-size ~660px`, repeating).

## Fonts
- **Proxima Nova** (web substitute in use: **DM Sans** — Light 300 / Regular 400 / Medium 500 / Bold 700) — the **workhorse**, carries almost everything: body, captions, ingredient lists; **caps + bold** for secondary titles & subtitles; **light tracked caps** for labels & data/numbers.
- **Fraunces** (Regular, optical sizing) — the **spotlight** face. The “Skin Lab” wordmark, and beyond the logo only the ONE element per layout that must stand out most: a marquee title, a hero ingredient / peptide name. **Never body, labels, or captions.**
